C. Explain the race condition using two threads
Suppose Thread A and Thread B both want seat number 5.
Step	Thread A	Thread B
1	Checks seat 5	
2	Sees seat available	
3		Checks seat 5
4		Sees seat available
5	Books seat 5	
6		Books seat 5
7	Increments counter	Increments counter

Both users believe they successfully booked the same seat.

This is called a race condition because the result depends on the timing and interleaving of threads.
D. Identify the critical section
The critical section is:
if (!booked[seat]) {
    booked[seat] = true;
    bookingsMade++;
}


This section must execute atomically because checking availability and booking the seat are two operations that must be treated as one indivisible operation.

